:: Carter Yard Play Waterguns [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh, I know what we should do!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> suddenly says. The two of you had been trying to come up with a game to play in his yard, looking at the various equipment and activities around. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> had suddenly had an idea as you asked him if he had any outdoor toys. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I’ll be right back! Wait here!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quickly sprints to the door, grabbing one of the nearby towels to quickly dry himself off, before dashing inside. You sit down in one of the poolside chairs and relax for a minute <span style="Color: LightGreen">before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> returns, holding a pair of colorful plastic guns.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Water guns!”</span> He says happily, handing you one of the identical blasters. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I have a bunch but grabbed the best ones. Let’s fill them up and have a battle!”</span> He suggests. You agree, walking over with <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to fill them up in the pool before asking what the goal of the battle will be. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We’ll both start on opposite sides of the yard and sneak around to try and hit the other person. Whoever hits the other the most wins!”</span> He smiles, proud of himself, as you can’t help but think about how the ‘rules’ of the game aren’t really concrete nor is what counts as ‘hitting’. Though you guess every game doesn’t need an overly explained rulebook. <span style="Color: LightGreen">This was more about having fun than winning.</span> <br>
<br>
Once both of your guns are full of ammo, you move to opposite sides of the yard. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> takes up residence near his treehouse, crouching behind the tree as you find a base around the back of the patio. This kept you both out of sight, though you quickly realized how unbalanced the yard was. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> has both the treehouse and jungle gym, plenty of locations for cover and to get the high ground. <span style="Color: Yellow">Meanwhile, you just had the deck chairs, a grill, and a small shed for cover. The space between your bases is mostly open, save for the pool. This wasn’t going to be an easy battle.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ready? Go!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> declares from the bottom of the tree house, signaling the start of the game. You had to decide what you were going to do. <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Take to the water<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You peek out from behind your cover to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quietly moving up the jungle gym, no doubt planning to get a better vantage point. So, you quickly take a deep breath and slip into the pool in order to move quickly without being in the open. Your plan relies on him not noticing you in the pool, either through you moving close to the sides and underwater or just not expecting you to take such a path. <br>
        <br>
        You have to come up for air a few times as you move slowly through the pool, doing so carefully and slowly not to make any noise. Whenever you do, you pause briefly and listen out. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t make a sound, and it would be too risky to pop your head out more to try and get a better view. You have no idea if he knows your plan or not, your only choice is to keep going. <br>
        <br>
        Eventually, you reach the other end of the water and slowly surface, peeking just slightly over the edge of the pool towards the jungle gym. The only thing you can see is the red of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s trunks, just barely visible as he keeps his gun trained towards the patio. It occasionally moves and surveys the entire backyard, but he doesn’t once come towards the pool. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Perfect!</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Swim",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        You carefully slip out of the water, cringing as the water patters onto the concrete, though <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> doesn’t seem to hear it. You then quietly sneak towards the jungle gym, moving just below where <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> is. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What is he doing?”</span> You hear the boy whisper, still glancing near the patio, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Is he trying to wait me out? Or did he sneak through the front yard?”</span> He thinks out loud to himself, checking every angle of the backyard and every possible way you could have gone. He even briefly looks towards the pool, <span style="Color: LightGreen">though it is too late for that as you quickly begin to climb the jungle gym to sneak up behind him.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"Carter Yard Play Waterguns 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Sneak around carefully<br>">>
    <<replace "#choice">>
        You peek out from behind your cover to see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> quietly moving up to the jungle gym, no doubt planning to get a better vantage point. So, you quickly rush over to the shed as quickly and quietly as possible. It wasn’t the best path, but every other path was too open. Sure, they had cover, but he’d be able to tell which way you were coming from, leaving you at the mercy of his aim. Your only hope was to get close to him without him noticing. <br>
        <br>
        So, you crouch behind the shed, glancing at the rows of bushes that line the fence of the yard. It wouldn’t be a pleasant, or even easy, route to take, but it would keep you obscured for your approach. You’d have to move slowly, however, as to not cause too much noise or movement that would attract <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s attention. So, you peek out once more and wait until the boy is looking away from you before slowly entering the bushes. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: Yellow">You quickly discover that moving through the bushes wasn’t as good as an idea as you thought. Not because it doesn’t work, because you are indeed able to get to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> on a slow and concealed path, but because it is very uncomfortable. Wet, dressed in your swimwear without shoes; these combine to make for a very unpleasant experience as you walk through the roots and leaves of the bushes, trying not to cringe whenever you step on a sharp stick or feel some cold dirt slip between your toes.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "Carter",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Swim",
                        Mouth: "Frown",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        But eventually, you reach the end and creep out to the back of the jungle gym, spotting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s bright red trunks indicating his location. You tiptoe over directly below <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, glancing up to see if there are any signs he saw you slip into the bushes. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“What is he doing?”</span> You hear the boy whisper, still glancing near the patio, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Is he trying to wait me out? Or did he sneak through the front yard?”</span> He thinks out loud to himself, checking every angle of the backyard and every possible way you could have gone. He even briefly looks towards the shed, <span style="Color: LightGreen">though it is too late for that as you quickly begin to climb the jungle gym to sneak up behind him.</span> <br>
        <br>
        <<include"Carter Yard Play Waterguns 2">>
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>

:: Carter Yard Play Waterguns 2 [nobr]

/* Intro */
You crouch down low and slowly begin to move up the jungle gym, careful not to make any sudden movements that may alert <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to your position. As you get closer to the boy, you can see his expression. He looks confused, still staring over at the patio as if wondering if you had fallen asleep there or just left. <span style="Color: Pink">It’s almost cute watching his brain trying to work it out as you inch closer and closer. Then, once you are close enough and the boy is totally lost in thought, you aim your water gun directly at his butt and fire.</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "Carter",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Swim",
                Mouth: "Frown",
                Blush: 3,
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Aaahhhh!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> screams and jumps to his feet as the no doubt cold water hits his rear end. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>!?”</span> He says in surprise, turning towards you and raising his gun. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You shoot him directly in the face in response, forcing the boy to drop his gun as he falls backwards and tries to cover his face.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ah! Okay, I surrender! I surrender!”</span> You hold your fire and pick up his gun, aiming both at the boy with a smile. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“H- how did you even-!?”</span> He asks, though your response is only to aim both guns down and shoot the boy directly in the crotch. <span style="Color: LightGreen">A truly humorous way to celebrate your victory.</span> <br>
<span style="color:Red">-Carter Energy</span><br>
<<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 10>>
<span style="color:Green">+Carter Fun</span><br>
<<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
<<needChange "Fun" 10>>
<<socialChange "Carter" 1>>
<br>
[[Continue|Carter House Backyard Swim]]
